       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. The maximum is 3200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1200 mg/day for OTC use without supervision.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1600 mg/day), or **1600 mg/day total** split into smaller doses\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
